'''''Euphrasia hirtella''''' is a species of [[flowering plant]] belonging to the family [[Orobanchaceae]].<ref name="POWO">{{cite web |title=Euphrasia hirtella Jord. ex Reut. {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:802574-1 |website=Plants of the World Online |access-date=15 February 2021 |language=en}}</ref>

''Euphrasia hirtella'' has a vast native range through humid mountains ranges in southern Europe, the Caucasus, the [[Alborz]] range in northern Iran, an immensely disjunct area in Siberia, and [[Himalayas]] east towards Korea.<ref>{{cite web |title=Euphrasia hirtella |url=http://www.floraiberica.es/floraiberica/texto/pdfs/13_144_24_Euphrasia.pdf |publisher=[[Flora Iberica]] |access-date=9 September 2021 |page=460}}</ref><ref name="POWO" />

